"poll_margin": null, "poll_sd": null, "poll_weight": 0.0, "fundamentals": {"margin": -2.63, "lean": -9.0, "environment": 8.2, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": -1.83}, "rating_margin": -12.11, "sigma_race": 6.5, "sigma_total": 7.26, "baseline_margin": -8.32, "analyst_adjustment": -1.68, "key_factors": ["District's R-leaning partisan baseline (PVI R+9) after redrawn maps", "Mealer's dominant fundraising and outside spending versus Gutierrez's minimal resources", "Expert ratings uniformly favor Republicans, mostly Likely R", "Prediction markets price Democratic chances near 17%"], "rationale": "The redrawn Houston-area district leans Republican by about nine points, and Alex Mealer, a Trump-endorsed nominee, has raised over $2 million with nearly $5 million in outside support, while Leticia Gutierrez has raised under $60,000. Expert ratings cluster at Likely R and markets give Democrats roughly a 17% chance, supporting a Republican margin near ten points.", "watch": "Any polling showing Gutierrez competitive, or a scandal or backlash around Mealer's comments on the Houston ICE shooting, could narrow the race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Texas's 9th District is a newly drawn, Republican-leaning Houston-area seat created by the state's partisan remapping. Alex Mealer won a contested GOP primary runoff with Donald Trump's endorsement and enters the general election with a large financial advantage, having raised over $2 million and drawn nearly $5 million in outside support. Democrat Leticia Gutierrez has raised only about $55,000 with no reported outside spending.\n\nNo general-election polling is available, so the outlook rests on the district's Republican lean, the lopsided resource gap, and expert ratings that uniformly favor Republicans, most calling the race Likely R. Prediction markets similarly price Democratic chances at roughly 17%. Mealer is the clear favorite, though the new district's untested electorate leaves some room for surprise.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0912, "margin": -8.44}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0891, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0766, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1178, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0737, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0642, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0775, "margin": -10.0}]}